  "evaluation": "All three correctly identify a genuine disagreement and select population as the primary reason: treated depression patients and healthy controls differ substantially from a sarcoidosis cohort. All appropriately flag outcome definition and study design as additional differences, without treating these as grounds for an apparent conflict. A ranks first for its explicit, field-grounded account of all three differences. C narrowly follows because its detail captures both population and depression definition; B is equally sound substantively but less specific in its detail.",
